n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488205 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488205 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225064" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488205 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488205 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5.5)$ given below, compute $P(1<X<7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0266\\,$ | $\\,0.0884\\,$ | $\\,0.2017\\,$ | $\\,0.3575\\,$ | $\\,0.5289\\,$ | $\\,0.6860\\,$ | $\\,0.8095\\,$ |\n\n$P(1<X<7)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488205 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3fd62c03-4c13-5eaa-a871-a2d0ae21b2c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488205 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X<7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X\\in \\{2,3,4,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(1<X<7) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(1<X<7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<7) & =F(6)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.6860-0.0266 \\\\  & =0.6594.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488206 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488206 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224999" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488206 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488206 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, compute $P(X<7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ | $\\,0.8666\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ | $\\,0.9682\\,$ |\n\n$P(X<7)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 175