b-3639-5408-81fe-d49741329753" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488242 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-0.3134 \\\\  & =0.6866.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488250 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488250 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225057" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488250 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488250 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(6.5)$ given below, compute $P(3\\le X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0430\\,$ | $\\,0.1118\\,$ | $\\,0.2237\\,$ | $\\,0.3690\\,$ | $\\,0.5265\\,$ | $\\,0.6728\\,$ | $\\,0.7916\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488250 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9431e7c-b663-534c-b1f2-e2cde30992c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488250 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X\\le 7) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X\\le 7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 7) & =F(7)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6728-0.0430 \\\\  & =0.6298.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488256 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488256 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488256 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(5<X<9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ | $\\,0.7166\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488256 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bfd17aa5-30fb-5cb9-aef8-99d3d322cf8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488256 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X<9) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\})+P(X\\in \\{6,7,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 5)+P(5<X<9) \\\\  & =F(5)+P(5<X<9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5<X<9) & =F(8)-F(5) \\\\  & =0.5925-0.1912 \\\\  & =0.4013.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488266 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488266 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488266 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488266 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3)$ given below, compute $P(1\\le X\\le 4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0498\\,$ | $\\,0.1991\\,$ | $\\,0.4232\\,$ | $\\,0.6472\\,$ | $\\,0.8153\\,$ | $\\,0.9161\\,$ | $\\,0.9665\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488266 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0dd1d6e-e305-5637-930e-c61c5f8b750e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488266 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\